WEBVTT

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.610
No way! Why, have all the houses around us disappeared?

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.230
Impossible. Am I dreaming, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.280
It's no dream.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.530
That hurt!

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.950
Aliens!

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.620
Our alien friends have invited us over!

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.700
Oh, no! Maybe there's no oxygen!

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.120
I wonder if they're from Venus?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.330
It could be the little gray men!

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.170
It looks like we're definitely in a different location...

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.630
Let's go outside!

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:28.670
Don't.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Atori...

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.010
Miho is right.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.130
Our surroundings didn't disappear.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.890
We've all been transported along with this entire house.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.060
Do you know where this is?

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.140
Yeah. It's Shangri-la.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.350
Shangri-la?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.400
Ai! Miho! Fujiwara!

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.110
I bet that deep down you actually do desire this happy world,

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.950
this Shangri-la.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.280
That's why you invited your friends here.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.290
You're wrong! I want to go back!

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.250
I've been wanting to go home, so...

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.050
So, then why not return them...

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.170
to their original world?

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:17.090
Please, go back to your original world!

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.020
It won't change now.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.350
Because you already wished for it.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.440
Because you saw them in this world,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.440
they are now established to exist in this world.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.080
Hang in there Haruka.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.670
I'll come and save you!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.310
Aren't you glad?

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.150
They will be freed from an unhappy future with...

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.280
their arrival in this dimension, The Shangri-la.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.280
It won't be just them.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.570
We shall save every future in every dimension!

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.330
You have the ability do it, Haruka.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.460
How can you tell that the future is unhappy?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:58.170
I have seen the futures of every dimension.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:04.220
Very well, I shall show you their future as well.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.350
Don't do it, you don't know what could happen.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.230
But we have to find Haruka.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.940
I can't just abandon Yuu!

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.820
Then do what you want!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.690
Uh-huh, we will do what we want.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.820
Hey, are you going with them?!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.900
Will you come with us, Atori?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.820
Damn...

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.030
What choice do I have?

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:27.990
Yay!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.790
Here goes.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.380
Their parents died five years ago, didn't they?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.720
That's the thing. The grandmother raised them in their place.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.260
So, what will those kids do now?

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.060
I heard they'll be taken in by distant relatives.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:54.060
I'm told Isami-chan will be taken in by a friend of his deceased father.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.770
It's a shame the brothers have to be split up like that.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.400
Fujiwara...

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.360
Ah, the chain of unhappiness has begun.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.650
What do you mean?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.200
This is only the beginning
of their unhappy future.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.920
Idiot!

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.090
Poor thing.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.550
She doesn't seem to have any friends.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.710
Who, Miho?!

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.670
And as for the others...

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.510
Hasebe-senpai!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.930
I heard that you made the all-star team!

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:33.890
Yeah.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.730
Wow, that's incredible! Give it your best!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:37.600
Thanks!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.610
I'll be watching you on TV for sure!

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.520
Get a goal, senpai!

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.860
Leave it to me! Thanks for your support!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.030
Of course!

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.070
Fujiwara?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.330
Oh no, it's the punks from North High.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:56.330
They've been making a name for themselves for being tough in fights.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.750
Senpai, do you know him?

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.630
Yeah. We were classmates in elementary school.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:09.430
Hmm?

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.470
You little...

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.640
Stop it! Stop it!

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.640
Isami, get it already!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:19.190
Let's beat it!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:19.850
Yeah!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.400
What do you think? Do you still consider this a happy future?

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.650
Fujiwara...

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.580
Miyuki! Miyuki!

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.250
Coming, hold on a second!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.330
It's gone. It's gone.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.840
What are you talking about, Asuka?

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.750
Just come with me!

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.260
What's wrong? What is it?

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.970
Look! It's gone!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.970
Gone? What's gone?

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.060
My house is gone!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.770
B-But how? How can a house be gone?!

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.350
I don't know! That's what I'd like to know!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.310
Oh, what's going on?!

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.570
Somebody explain it to me!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.820
I forgot! Haruka was in the house!

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.820
Haruka was in there! Where is she?!

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.910
Calm down, Asuka!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:24.920
Yuu...

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.470
What is it?

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.180
It looked far away a while ago,

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.180
but we've come pretty close.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.060
You know, the mountain that looks like a castle.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.440
What are you talking about... It's still a long way off.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.400
Where are you looking at, Karasu?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.530
See? You can see it right over there.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.610
Does it appear close by to you?

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.950
Can't you see it?

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.280
No.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.710
I see. Maybe it's because this space is decoherent.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:02.500
Huh?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.210
It's the same as when you split into two at La'cryma.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.630
This place is also indistinct without an established existence.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.050
So, what I'm seeing is an illusion?

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:19.390
Not really. Your strong desire to save Haruka

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.560
has established this indistinct space.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.810
So, if I think about her even harder...

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.020
...the path will begin to open.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.070
Get down!

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.630
That's a bit harsh, Isami.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.550
We're working hard too, y'know?

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.060
Yeah.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.100
Geez. You guys...

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:05.140
Isami, just listen to me.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.400
The thing is, my girl said...

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.400
Fujiwara.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.610
Oh, it's you.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.740
Long time no see.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.030
Huh? Well, yeah.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.860
Who's this? A friend of yours?

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.030
What are you doing?

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.740
What am I doing?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.200
I'm on the way home from soccer practice.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:28.330
Oh, so you're still playing that soccer 'bullshit'.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.090
And what are YOU doing?

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.380
That's none of your business.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.180
Do you understand what you're doing?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.470
Acting tough doesn't suit you!

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:40.640
Are you lecturing me?

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.390
What I do is my business!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:44.600
It's wrong!

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.390
Shut up. Get lost!

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:52.650
You just don't get it... you just don't...

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:55.860
Go away.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.410
Hey there.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:09.000
I hear you guys have been very naughty recently.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.460
Well, we need to have a little talk.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:16.340
Get up!

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.140
Where you think you're going?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:29.190
Take a good look at your opponent before picking a fight. Got it?!

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.940
They've probably had enough.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:34.860
Let's get outta here.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.900
What're you talking about, Isami?

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.240
We have to be thorough, or...

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.580
What's the deal?!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.920
Don't give me this crap.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.510
You want a piece of me?!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.380
Then do it!

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.180
What? Are you all show?!

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.470
Don't you intimidate me!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:10.730
You want more beating?! Eh.. you bastard?!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.600
Hey, knock it off.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.730
That's fine by me, bastard! Let's get it on!

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:17.280
I said, knock it off!

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:20.990
Huh?!

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.420
L... Let's get outta here.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.300
Yeah.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.300
This is bad. This is really bad!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.180
This is really, fucking bad!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.100
Fujiwara...

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:51.810
The poor thing.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.980
He's been abandoned by his friends.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.030
Impossible.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:05.120
There are five laboratory ships in all.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:09.660
They will align around this mountain in a
circle and launch elementary particles.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.870
The five ships will be used to accelerate the particles,

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.880
forcing the quantum potential to bend along the circle.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:21.510
They will launch three types of particles: Alpha, beta, and gamma,

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:25.050
which will be accelerated in the Magic Circle
until they achieve the speed of light.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.220
When every particle has achieved the speed of light,

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:31.770
the dimension will arrive at the critical point,
where theta particles will be produced.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.940
I see. It's slightly
different from our history.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.320
In what way?

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:41.360
I think the history is happening 5 years faster.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:44.610
Is that due to a violation of causality

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.950
rather than this being an approximate dimension?

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:47.910
Probably.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:52.250
Hey, you two. Don't you think that's enough of the complex stuff?

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:56.880
All we really need is to destroy that thing, right?

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.210
An '85 Romanée-Conte.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.720
Its flavor is described as mysterious.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:09.050
It's known as the greatest beverage created by man.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.350
How about it, Mayuzumi-chan?

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.390
Don't you agree it's a suitable wine for this historic event?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:18.360
Shinohara-kun, I will warn you once again.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:19.770
Stop the experiment.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:22.190
Now, now... Don't get so worked up.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.780
Thanks to your pointing out this place, the Magic Circle should work.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.160
Thanks.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.620
You okay?

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.750
Kooriyama-san?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.920
I'm not too keen on floating in midair,

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.880
but once my feet are on solid ground, I'm fine.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.090
No! Even if you start that...

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:46.760
It's fine. It's a path mankind is bound to take someday anyway.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.390
Drink up!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.350
If I don't do it, someone else will.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:58.100
The thing about mankind is, we always want to get ahead.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.270
We're not happy with things the way they are.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.230
That's why we remember the guys who got ahead of us

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:04.530
with admiration and jealousy.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:08.860
For as long as humans exist...

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:13.240
I will be remembered as the one who created a new era.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:30.430
That's funny. It seems like it's farther away now.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:31.510
It's fear.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.480
The fear in you has pushed Haruka away.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.270
It's me?

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.980
If you want to save her, don't run away. Stand and face it.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.070
All right, Karasu.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:55.290
I heard he lost sight in one eye in a knife fight.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.620
No way. Was it those guys we saw?

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:00.920
Yeah. I think it was the one that Hasebe-senpai said she knew.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.130
Wow.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.630
Oh, Senpai...

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.460
You're kidding about Fujiwara, right?

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.630
Uhh, Senpai!

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.510
Ow...

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:17.600
Are you okay?

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:19.350
I... I'm fine.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:20.890
Ow!

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:28.690
Miho?

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.160
Miho! You've been in there long enough, now come out!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.280
You've been shut in there for 2 weeks now!

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.120
Can you hear me?! Miho!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:49.920
Um, doctor?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.090
I have a soccer game coming up soon.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.510
Will it heal soon?

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.350
I want you to listen to me calmly.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.490
I'm saying that you must now give up soccer.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:23.120
The fact of the matter is, if we don't amputate your left leg,

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.040
within the next three months, you may lose your life.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:29.210
Miho? Please come out, Miho.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.590
Miho...

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.890
Who are... you?

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.490
Clearly, it is a depersonalization disorder.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:39.740
I suspect that it stems from her desire to deny reality,

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.790
due to extreme stress.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.650
Stop it!

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.150
Everybody, stop it!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.940
I hate this future!

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:17.820
I told you. The future contains nothing but unhappiness.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.740
But <i>you</i> wanted to see

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.540
the so-called 'possibilities' the future had to offer.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.370
I will never believe it.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.710
Not this future!

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.880
Then would you like to see more of the future?

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.250
No!

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:38.840
You, Haruka, are the only one who can cut away this future.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.220
With your Dragon Torque power,

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:46.850
you can change every unhappy future into Shangri-la.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.230
I can?

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:52.610
That's right... and once you do that...

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.820
there will never be another unhappy future for all eternity.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:07.830
What is it?

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.540
It's Haruka...

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:10.960
Haruka?

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.420
She said "Help everyone."

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:15.380
"Everyone."

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.430
Isami.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.230
What're you doing, Isami?

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:30.310
Yuu?

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.100
Stop it. It's not like you.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.980
What are you doing here?

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.030
When did you come back from Tokyo?!

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.950
Come on. Go to Hasebe.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.990
You're the only one who can save her, Isami.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:46.490
Me?

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.700
Isami, who else can do it?

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:51.410
Yuu...

00:19:58.210 --> 00:19:59.300
Miho.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.880
I've been looking for you...

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:03.720
So this is where you wandered off to.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.680
Who are you?

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.810
Let's go home, back to where the guys are.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:11.940
No.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:15.190
This isn't where you belong.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.560
You know that.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.070
Hasebe!

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.740
Fujiwara?

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:28.660
Don't stand there, it's dangerous! Come here!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.370
What did you come here for?

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.120
Did you come here to laugh at me?

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:37.340
Did you come here to laugh at me 'cause I can't play soccer

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:38.670
or even walk anymore?

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:42.510
You idiot! What's one leg?!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.090
Look at me, I lost an eye.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.260
I'm done here.

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:50.970
You're not done!

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.190
I can't be your legs,

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:58.360
but if you want to run, I'll run with you on my back!

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.650
I'll play soccer with you on my back!

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.240
So, please...

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:09.490
Please, Hasebe...

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:12.000
Come over here.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.370
Fujiwara...

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.840
Everyone is waiting.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.090
Everyone?

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.890
You are not alone.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.220
C'mon, let's go.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.490
It's all right. They're all safe.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.280
Good.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:50.200
Let's go.

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:52.540
This time, I'll find Haruka.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:54.000
For sure!

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:58.580
Fujiwara?

00:21:58.750 --> 00:21:59.750
Hasebe.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.130
I... I was dreaming.

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:04.050
Me too.

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:05.550
Atori?

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:07.590
It was no dream.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:12.390
That was a future dimension that was consumed by Shangri-la.

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:14.890
That was our future?

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:17.270
One possible future.

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:22.110
They're... They're all back.

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:24.860
The future isn't set in stone.

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:27.150
Even if we encounter unhappiness in the future,

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:29.070
we will not give up!

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:39.790
But one of you couldn't endure the misfortune.

00:22:40.120 --> 00:22:42.500
Do you know who it was?

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:44.300
It was Yuu.

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:46.760
The future Goto Yuu.

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:50.930
You already realize that, don't you?

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:55.010
I...

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:58.520
am the Yuu of this dimension.

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:00.560
Haruka...

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:05.190
You left me behind,

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:07.110
and died.

00:24:42.210 --> 00:24:44.330
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:46.920
That summer day's dream.

00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:52.050
All dimensions will unite, and expire.

00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:57.350
Yuu! Do not fear! Think only of Haruka.

00:24:59.720 --> 00:25:03.430
I don't know that for sure... but I can save Haruka!

00:25:04.060 --> 00:25:06.150
Next episode, The End.

00:25:07.310 --> 00:25:09.820
Is everyone going to disappear?
